Assumptions: the book of 31 Dec 2025 held constant; floating
rates move with the policy rate one for one (cards, overdrafts,
SME term, variable mortgages, companies); funding costs
0.55 + 0.72 x policy rate (fitted), anchored to today's 3.25%,
on everything CET1 does not fund; costs half of 2025's net
interest income, $95.6m a year; no fees, tax or dividends.

